  <prompt>
    Add optional `rowHeight?: string` field to `LayoutJsonRow` schema (Dataverse `sprk_workspacelayout.sprk_sectionsjson`). Wire the framework so a row with `rowHeight` set is clamped to that height and sections inside respect the ceiling regardless of `contentSizing`. Ship unit tests covering set + omitted cases + interaction with `contentSizing`.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE frontend framework developer. Extends the workspace layout schema.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `LayoutJsonRow.rowHeight?: string` field exists; framework applies it as a height ceiling on the row wrapper; interaction with section-level `contentSizing` documented + tested; back-compat verified.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      A widget that needs 480px in a multi-section dashboard needs 800px+ in a single-section full-page layout. Today, one hardcoded `defaultHeight` baked into section metadata — no per-layout variation. FR-02 adds `rowHeight` at the layout level as the per-instance override.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/types/</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WorkspaceShell/buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Framework changes stay in `@spaarke/ui-components`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">Shared-lib code React-16-safe.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Additive; omitted `rowHeight` = current behavior (sections apply own contentSizing).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/spec.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/embedded-widget-sizing.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read spec.md § FR-02. Locate `LayoutJsonRow` type definition.</step>
    <step order="2">Add `readonly rowHeight?: string;` field with JSDoc: `Optional. When set, this row is clamped to the height (accepts any CSS length: '480px', '80vh', '100vh'). Sections respect this ceiling regardless of their contentSizing.`</step>
    <step order="3">Update `buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig.ts` (or the row-building step) to apply `rowHeight` as `maxHeight` on the row wrapper `style`, along with `overflow: hidden` (to guarantee section overflow behavior).</step>
    <step order="4">Document interaction: when both `rowHeight` set on row AND `contentSizing: 'clamped'` set on section, the row's ceiling wins; section's `defaultHeight` no longer applies (row already provides the constraint).</step>
    <step order="5">Unit test: (a) row without `rowHeight` renders as today, (b) row with `rowHeight: '80vh'` gets `maxHeight: '80vh'` on wrapper, (c) row with `rowHeight` set + section with `contentSizing: 'clamped'` — verify section's `defaultHeight` doesn't over-constrain (row wins).</step>
    <step order="6">`npm test` + `npm run build` — clean.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: → ✅.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build + test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/types/{LayoutJsonRow-location}.ts (modified)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WorkspaceShell/buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig.ts (modified)</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WorkspaceShell/__tests__/buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig.test.ts (extended)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a row with `rowHeight: '80vh'`, when the workspace renders, then the row wrapper `style.maxHeight === '80vh'`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a row without `rowHeight`, when the workspace renders, then no `maxHeight` is applied by the row (sections apply own contentSizing per FR-01).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a row with `rowHeight` + a section with `contentSizing: 'clamped'`, when the workspace renders, then the row's `maxHeight` is authoritative; section's `defaultHeight` is not applied as an additional constraint.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Unit tests + build clean.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    - This is the schema half of FR-02. The wizard UI (task 011) exposes the field to makers.
    - Framework only enforces height at the row level; overflow behavior lives on the DataGrid's inner scroll surface per existing height-chain contract.
    - COMPLETION NOTES (2026-07-02, task-execute FULL rigor):
      • `LayoutJsonRow` located in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WorkspaceShell/buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig.ts` (co-located with `LayoutJson` and `WorkspaceScope`, NOT under `src/types/`).
      • Added `readonly rowHeight?: string;` field with JSDoc documenting the contentSizing interaction.
      • Extended `WorkspaceRowConfig` in `types.ts` with `maxHeight?: string;` + `overflow?: React.CSSProperties['overflow'];` fields (framework-internal contract populated by `buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig`).
      • Wired `buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig.ts` to propagate `rowHeight` → `{ maxHeight, overflow: 'hidden' }` on the row wrapper. Propagates to overflow-split rows too.
      • Wired `WorkspaceShell.tsx` row `<div>` to apply `row.maxHeight` and `row.overflow` on inline style.
      • Added 4 new tests (f)/(g)/(h)/(i) covering: back-compat (omitted rowHeight), rowHeight set, interaction with `contentSizing: 'clamped'`, and overflow-row propagation.
      • Interaction: when both `rowHeight` (row) AND `contentSizing: 'clamped'` (section) are set, both apply — row `maxHeight` + `overflow: hidden` is authoritative on the wrapper; section's own `maxHeight` (from FR-01 clamped) still applies on the inner card style. The row's `overflow: hidden` ensures no over-constraint. Test (h) verifies this contract explicitly.
      • Tests: 10/10 buildDynamicWorkspaceConfig tests pass (6 FR-01 + 4 FR-02).
      • Build: `tsc` clean (no output).
      • Pre-existing failures in unrelated files (EntityCreationService, XrmDataverseClient, RichFilePreview, sectionMetadataCatalog — task 014's territory) are NOT caused by this task.
  </notes>

